BT /F2 10.50 Tf ET
BT 59.53 722.17 Td (This standard describes how passwords for Halvenroot accounts are chosen, protected and managed,) Tj ET
BT 59.53 707.28 Td (and how Halvenroot systems protect the sign-in process against guessing attacks.) Tj ET
BT 59.53 685.31 Td (It applies to all employees, contractors and any other personnel who have an account on a Halvenroot) Tj ET
BT 59.53 670.43 Td (system, whether that system is in a Halvenroot office, a warehouse site or a hosted service that) Tj ET
BT 59.53 655.55 Td (Halvenroot uses. It covers user passwords. Multi-factor authentication is set by the Multi-Factor) Tj ET
BT 59.53 640.67 Td (Authentication Standard, and privileged credentials are set by the Privileged Access Standard.) Tj ET
BT 59.53 618.70 Td (This version replaces version 1.0, which took effect on 2024-03-01.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13.00 Tf ET
BT 59.53 588.54 Td (2 Roles) Tj ET
BT 70.87 569.80 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (- ) Tj /F1 10.50 Tf (Every user) Tj /F2 10.50 Tf ( follows this standard, protects their own passwords and reports any password they) Tj ET
BT 70.87 554.92 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (believe has been exposed.) Tj ET
BT 70.87 537.20 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (- ) Tj /F1 10.50 Tf (The IAM team) Tj /F2 10.50 Tf ( configures the identity portal so that it enforces the rules in sections 4 and 5, and) Tj ET
BT 70.87 522.32 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (maintains the password blocklist.) Tj ET
BT 70.87 504.61 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (- ) Tj /F1 10.50 Tf (System owners) Tj /F2 10.50 Tf ( make sure that the systems they own, where they keep their own passwords,) Tj ET
BT 70.87 489.72 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (meet the same rules.) Tj ET
BT 70.87 472.01 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (- ) Tj /F1 10.50 Tf (Resource owners) Tj /F2 10.50 Tf ( decide who may use the resources they own and grant that access to) Tj ET
BT 70.87 457.13 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (individual accounts.) Tj ET
BT 70.87 439.41 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (- ) Tj /F1 10.50 Tf (The IT Service Desk) Tj /F2 10.50 Tf ( helps users with sign-in problems and with the self-service reset. It never) Tj ET
BT 70.87 424.53 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (asks a user for their password.) Tj ET
BT 70.87 406.81 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (- ) Tj /F1 10.50 Tf (The Security Operations Centre) Tj /F2 10.50 Tf ( receives reports of exposed or compromised passwords and) Tj ET
BT 70.87 391.93 Td /F2 10.50 Tf (decides what further action is needed.) Tj ET
