BT 59.53 579.93 Td (4.6 Protecting passwords) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.50 Tf ET
BT 59.53 562.01 Td (All passwords are confidential information. Never share your password with anyone, including the IT) Tj ET
BT 59.53 547.13 Td (Service Desk. If someone asks you for your password, refuse and tell the Security Operations Centre.) Tj ET
BT 59.53 525.16 Td (Do not write passwords down, and do not keep them in email, chat messages or notes. Store work) Tj ET
BT 59.53 510.28 Td (passwords only in the approved password manager; its autofill feature may be used. Do not reuse a) Tj ET
BT 59.53 495.39 Td (Halvenroot password for any other account, work or personal.) Tj ET
BT 59.53 473.43 Td (If a colleague needs access to your work while you are away, the resource owner grants them their) Tj ET
BT 59.53 458.54 Td (own access.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf ET
BT 59.53 430.40 Td (4.7 Self-service reset) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.50 Tf ET
BT 59.53 412.48 Td (Self-service password reset in the Halvenroot identity portal requires MFA. Security questions are not) Tj ET
BT 59.53 397.60 Td (used. If you cannot complete the self-service reset, contact the IT Service Desk, which verifies your) Tj ET
BT 59.53 382.72 Td (identity before helping you.) Tj ET

